WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.470 line:0
Rapid burial protects a shell from destruction.

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:10.400 line:0
Dissolution then removes the shell, leaving a shaped cavity

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:11.140 line:0
called a mold.

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:17.980 line:0
Later minerals fill that cavity, producing a cast that

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:19.380 line:0
reproduces the shell's shape.

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:26.140 line:0
These are different records: the mold is an empty

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:29.500 line:0
impression, while the cast is its later infill. This

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:32.480 line:0
is one fossil-preservation route, not the fate of every

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:32.740 line:0
fossil.
